========================
3) Booking Features (Ride Scheduling / Pre-Booking / Cancel Rule)
========================

3.1 Create Ride (Immediate OR Scheduled)
POST /Orders
Body: CreateOrderDto (already existing)
Important:
- If Date is far in the future (Date > now + ScheduledDispatchLeadTimeMinutes),
  the order is created with Status = "scheduled" and drivers ARE notified immediately as a scheduled ride.
- Otherwise the order is created with Status = "pending" and drivers are notified (existing behavior).

3.1.1 Driver accepts scheduled ride (pre-assigned)
PUT /Orders/driver
Body:
{
  "orderId": 0,
  "driverid": 0,
  "status": "scheduled_accepted"
}
Effect:
- Status => "scheduled_accepted"
- DriverId => accepted driver
Notes:
- Backend prevents driver from accepting another scheduled ride that conflicts in time
  (uses ScheduledConflictWindowMinutes).

3.2 List Scheduled Orders for a User
GET /Orders/user/{userId}/scheduled
Response 200: List<OrderDto> (Status can be "scheduled" / "scheduled_accepted" / "pending" for upcoming scheduled rides)

3.3 Cancel Order (Scheduled cancellation cutoff)
PUT /Orders/user/cancel
Body:
{
  "orderId": 0,
  "userId": "string"
}
Rule:
- If Status == "scheduled" or "scheduled_accepted" then cancellation is allowed only BEFORE
  (order.Date - ScheduledCancelCutoffMinutes).
Defaults (can be changed in appsettings.json -> OrderSettings):
- ScheduledDispatchLeadTimeMinutes = 10
- ScheduledCancelCutoffMinutes = 15
- ScheduledReminderMinutes = 60
- ScheduledStartingSoonMinutes = 10
- ScheduledConflictWindowMinutes = 60

3.4 Automatic reminders + "starting soon" transition (background service)
Every 1 minute backend checks:
- Orders where Status = "scheduled_accepted" and Date <= now + ScheduledReminderMinutes
  => sends reminder notification to the accepted driver (once per runtime).
- Orders where Status = "scheduled_accepted" and Date <= now + ScheduledStartingSoonMinutes
  => Status becomes "pending" and notifies user + driver ("Ride Starting Soon").
